What the rewrite changed
------------------------

The original behaviour is untouched: a creeper that is about to explode refuses to die, a creeper
that is hurt by another creeper swells up and remembers it with a "Boom" flag, creepers walk to the
nearest free spider and ride it, creepers open doors while hunting, and creepers search nearby
block entities and blow them up. Those goals and the hurt hook were kept, but the code moved:

* the creeper hurt handling lives in event/CreeperCombatHandler,
* the "ride the nearest spider" goal became a reusable ai/goal/MountNearestEntityGoal,
* the "walk to an explodable block entity" goal became ai/goal/SeekExplodableBlockGoal with a
  pluggable swell controller, and its block lookup is shared through util/TargetFinder,
* the mixins only add the goals and keep the Boom/fire swell handling.

Added on top of that: chain detonation for creepers, a split tag that spawning creepers roll for and
that makes a tagged creeper spawn two already igniting creepers when it dies, naturally spawned
phantoms that may carry a mounted wither
skeleton, skeleton, pillager or evoker, arrows of the phantom riding wither skeleton that apply
wither, blindness and fire, arrows of the phantom riding skeleton that apply Instant Damage,
phantom bombardment with TNT or fireballs, and vindicators that spawn riding a chicken. Everything
is configurable - the new mechanics as well as the numbers the original mod had hard coded.

Port history
------------

1.4.0 fixes a server crash that happened when a creeper with the split tag detonated: the chain
detonation and the split children were triggered directly from inside the explosion start event, so
the explosion code ran re-entrantly. Those follow ups are now queued to the end of the server tick,
the block-entity swell value is clamped, and the phantom bombardment gained its two stage AI.

1.5.0 adds the potion phantom with its own AI, the explosive and lava arrow tags for skeletons, the
cat reaction of creepers and the looting behaviour of endermen. Every event handler now catches its
own failures and reports them without going through log4j, because a broken log4j configuration used
to replace the real exception with a LinkageError during crash reporting.

1.6.0 fixes what the first pass got wrong: the potion phantom throws its volley at the player instead
of straight down, watches a 16 block radius, keeps enough distance so its own splash potions cannot
hit it, and is explicitly exclusive with the TNT and fireball payloads. The enderman now turns the
block it carries into dirt instead of filling the hole back in. The explosive and lava arrow effects
run at the end of the tick so they can no longer re-enter the explosion code, and the valuable block
search is throttled because it scans nine chunks at once.

1.7.0 makes chain detonation the highest priority of a detonating creeper - the original blast is
cancelled so a creeper can never go off a second time - adds self damage immunity for everything the
mod causes, makes the potion phantom chase at a low 3 to 7 block altitude, and turned every remaining
hard coded number into a config option.
